<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#09090b" />
    <title><%= title %> · ActorLab</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/project.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="shell">
      <aside class="sidebar">
        <a class="brand" href="#top"
          ><span class="brand-mark">A</span
          ><span
            >Actor<span class="brand-light">Lab</span
            ><small>RUNTIME FIELD GUIDE</small></span
          ></a
        >
        <div class="side-label">PROJECT</div>
        <a class="side-link active" href="#overview"
          ><span class="nav-icon">◈</span>Overview</a
        >
        <div class="side-label">HOW IT WORKS</div>
        <a class="side-link" href="#architecture"
          ><span class="nav-icon">⌘</span>Architecture</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#message-flow"
          ><span class="nav-icon">↗</span>Message flow</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#state"
          ><span class="nav-icon">▤</span>Actor state</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#workers"
          ><span class="nav-icon">▦</span>Workers &amp; placement</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#rebalance"
          ><span class="nav-icon">⇄</span>Rebalancing</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#singletons"
          ><span class="nav-icon">◇</span>Singletons</a
        >
        <div class="side-label">OPERATIONS</div>
        <a class="side-link" href="#kubernetes"
          ><span class="nav-icon">☸</span>Kubernetes</a
        >
        <a class="side-link" href="#local-dev"
          ><span class="nav-icon">⌘</span>Local development</a
        >
        <div class="sidebar-bottom">
          <span class="live-dot"></span><span>Runtime guide</span
          ><span class="version">v1.0</span>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <main id="top" class="main">
        <header class="topbar">
          <div class="crumb">ActorLab <span>/</span> Project guide</div>
          <a class="github-link" href="#architecture"
            ><span>⌘</span> Runtime architecture <span class="arrow">↗</span></a
          >
        </header>
        <div class="content">
          <section id="overview" class="hero">
            <div class="eyebrow">
              <span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> VIRTUAL ACTOR RUNTIME
              <span class="eyebrow-line"></span> KUBERNETES READY
            </div>
            <h1>Actors that keep<br />their <span>identity.</span></h1>
            <p class="hero-copy">
              ActorLab is a small, distributed runtime for stateful virtual
              actors. It routes each message to the actor’s current worker,
              saves state durably, and moves actors as the worker pool changes.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button primary" href="#message-flow"
                >Explore the runtime <span>↓</span></a
              ><a class="button secondary" href="#local-dev"
                >Run locally <span>↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
            <div class="hero-foot">
              <span><i class="status-dot green"></i> Durable actor state</span
              ><span><i class="status-dot blue"></i> Distributed ownership</span
              ><span><i class="status-dot amber"></i> Kubernetes aware</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-index">01 / 08</div>
          </section>

          <section class="stats" aria-label="Runtime building blocks">
            <article class="stat">
              <span class="stat-icon blue-icon">◈</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Virtual actors</strong
                ><small>Identity independent of workers</small>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-index">01</span>
            </article>
            <article class="stat">
              <span class="stat-icon green-icon">▤</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Durable state</strong
                ><small>MongoDB is the source of truth</small>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-index">02</span>
            </article>
            <article class="stat">
              <span class="stat-icon amber-icon">⇄</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Live placement</strong
                ><small>Redis coordinates ownership</small>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-index">03</span>
            </article>
            <article class="stat">
              <span class="stat-icon slate-icon">☸</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Cluster native</strong
                ><small>Workers scale as pods</small>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-index">04</span>
            </article>
          </section>

          <section id="architecture" class="section-block">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">SYSTEM MAP <span>01</span></div>
                <h2>One identity. A distributed runtime.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                Actor IDs are stable. Worker placement is temporary and can
                change without changing how a client addresses an actor.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="architecture panel">
              <div class="diagram-label">ACTORLAB · RUNTIME COMPONENTS</div>
              <div class="diagram-row clients">
                <div class="node client-node">
                  <span class="node-icon">⌘</span><b>Client / UI</b
                  ><small>HTTP requests</small>
                </div>
                <div class="connector arrow-right">
                  <span>actorId + message</span>
                </div>
                <div class="node api-node">
                  <span class="node-icon">⌁</span><b>ActorLab API</b
                  ><small>Express · routing · pages</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="diagram-row middle">
                <div class="node redis-node">
                  <span class="node-icon">◉</span><b>Redis</b
                  ><small>Owners · leases · queues</small>
                </div>
                <div class="connector double">
                  <span>lookup / coordinate</span>
                </div>
                <div class="node workers-node">
                  <span class="node-icon">▦</span><b>Actor workers</b
                  ><small>Mailboxes · handlers</small>
                  <div class="worker-pills">
                    <i></i><i></i><i></i><em>+N</em>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="connector arrow-right">
                  <span>load / save</span>
                </div>
                <div class="node mongo-node">
                  <span class="node-icon">◌</span><b>MongoDB</b
                  ><small>Durable actor state</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="diagram-note">
                <span class="live-dot"></span> Placement can move. Actor
                identity and persisted state stay addressable.
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="legend">
              <span><i class="legend-dot blue"></i>Request path</span
              ><span><i class="legend-dot amber"></i>Coordination</span
              ><span><i class="legend-dot green"></i>Durable storage</span>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="message-flow" class="section-block">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">
                  THE REQUEST PATH <span>02</span>
                </div>
                <h2>From message to saved state.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                A message is routed by actor identity. The worker serializes
                that actor’s work, applies its behavior, and persists the new
                version.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-grid">
              <article class="flow-card">
                <span class="step-no">01</span>
                <div class="flow-icon blue-icon">↗</div>
                <h3>Address the actor</h3>
                <p>
                  A client sends an actor ID and operation, such as
                  <code>counter-42</code> + <code>increment</code>.
                </p>
                <span class="flow-tag">IDENTITY</span>
              </article>
              <article class="flow-card">
                <span class="step-no">02</span>
                <div class="flow-icon amber-icon">⌕</div>
                <h3>Resolve ownership</h3>
                <p>
                  The router checks Redis for the current worker and its
                  ownership generation. If needed, the actor is assigned and
                  activated.
                </p>
                <span class="flow-tag">REDIS LOOKUP</span>
              </article>
              <article class="flow-card">
                <span class="step-no">03</span>
                <div class="flow-icon slate-icon">≋</div>
                <h3>Process in order</h3>
                <p>
                  The worker places the message in that actor’s mailbox.
                  Messages for one actor run sequentially, avoiding concurrent
                  state changes.
                </p>
                <span class="flow-tag">ACTOR MAILBOX</span>
              </article>
              <article class="flow-card">
                <span class="step-no">04</span>
                <div class="flow-icon green-icon">✓</div>
                <h3>Save and respond</h3>
                <p>
                  The handler updates state, writes a versioned state update to
                  MongoDB, records the result, then responds to the caller.
                </p>
                <span class="flow-tag">MONGODB WRITE</span>
              </article>
            </div>
            <div class="note-bar">
              <span class="note-symbol">i</span>
              <p>
                <b>Delivery guarantee:</b> practical at-least-once processing.
                Message IDs and idempotency checks help reject retries; the
                runtime does not claim exactly-once delivery.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="state" class="section-block split-section">
            <div>
              <div class="section-kicker">ACTOR MODEL <span>03</span></div>
              <h2>Small state machines<br />with durable memory.</h2>
              <p class="section-copy">
                An actor owns its state and defines the operations that can
                change it. The runtime can deactivate an actor in memory and
                restore it later from its durable record.
              </p>
              <div class="actor-types">
                <div class="type-row">
                  <span class="type-symbol blue-icon">#</span>
                  <div>
                    <b>CounterActor</b
                    ><small>increment · decrement · get</small>
                  </div>
                  <code>{ count: 12 }</code>
                </div>
                <div class="type-row">
                  <span class="type-symbol green-icon">$</span>
                  <div>
                    <b>BankAccountActor</b
                    ><small>deposit · withdraw · getBalance</small>
                  </div>
                  <code>{ balance: 250 }</code>
                </div>
                <div class="type-row">
                  <span class="type-symbol amber-icon">◷</span>
                  <div>
                    <b>GlobalSchedulerActor</b
                    ><small>singleton · scheduled work</small>
                  </div>
                  <code>{ jobs: 4 }</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="state-panel panel">
              <div class="code-head">
                <span><i class="live-dot"></i> ACTOR RECORD</span
                ><span>MongoDB</span>
              </div>
              <pre><span class="code-muted">{</span>
  <span class="code-key">"actorId"</span>: <span class="code-string">"counter-42"</span>,
  <span class="code-key">"actorType"</span>: <span class="code-string">"CounterActor"</span>,
  <span class="code-key">"state"</span>: { <span class="code-key">"count"</span>: <span class="code-number">12</span> },
  <span class="code-key">"status"</span>: <span class="code-string">"active"</span>,
  <span class="code-key">"workerId"</span>: <span class="code-string">"worker-b"</span>,
  <span class="code-key">"version"</span>: <span class="code-number">8</span>,
  <span class="code-key">"lastActiveAt"</span>: <span class="code-string">"…"</span>
<span class="code-muted">}</span></pre>
              <div class="code-foot">
                <span>Persisted state survives worker restarts.</span
                ><span class="version-check">VERSIONED ✓</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="workers" class="section-block">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">
                  PLACEMENT &amp; RECOVERY <span>04</span>
                </div>
                <h2>Workers are replaceable. Actors aren’t.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                Workers host active actor instances, but they don’t own the only
                copy of actor state. Redis tracks placement; MongoDB makes
                recovery possible.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="worker-grid">
              <article class="worker-card panel">
                <div class="card-head">
                  <span class="worker-avatar">W1</span
                  ><span class="badge online">HEALTHY</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Worker process</h3>
                <p>
                  Registers a worker ID, renews its heartbeat, accepts actor
                  assignments, and exposes a health endpoint.
                </p>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Heartbeat</span><b>periodic</b>
                </div>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Active actors</span><b>reported to registry</b>
                </div>
              </article>
              <article class="worker-card panel">
                <div class="card-head">
                  <span class="worker-avatar alt">↻</span
                  ><span class="badge durable">RECOVERY</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Failure recovery</h3>
                <p>
                  When a heartbeat expires, the coordinator marks the worker
                  unavailable and reassigns its actors to healthy workers.
                </p>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Reload</span><b>latest MongoDB state</b>
                </div>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Fence</span><b>reject stale ownership</b>
                </div>
              </article>
              <article class="worker-card panel">
                <div class="card-head">
                  <span class="worker-avatar blue-avatar">⇄</span
                  ><span class="badge balanced">PLACEMENT</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Actor distribution</h3>
                <p>
                  A simple actor-count strategy spreads assignments across
                  available workers. Actor IDs remain unchanged as placement
                  shifts.
                </p>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Registry</span><b>Redis ownership map</b>
                </div>
                <div class="worker-meta">
                  <span>Identity</span><b>stable actor ID</b>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="rebalance" class="section-block">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">SAFE MIGRATION <span>05</span></div>
                <h2>Move ownership in a controlled handoff.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                Rebalancing evens out actor counts after workers join or leave.
                Each move preserves state and prevents the old owner from
                continuing to process.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="rebalance-panel panel">
              <div class="rebalance-top">
                <div>
                  <span class="badge balanced">REBALANCE SEQUENCE</span>
                  <h3>Drain → persist → transfer → resume</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="balance-before">
                  <span>BEFORE</span>
                  <div><i style="width: 82%"></i></div>
                  <b>W1 · 82</b>
                  <div><i class="bar-two" style="width: 31%"></i></div>
                  <b>W2 · 31</b>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="sequence">
                <div class="sequence-item">
                  <span>1</span><b>Select</b
                  ><small>Choose actors from overloaded workers.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="sequence-item">
                  <span>2</span><b>Drain</b
                  ><small>Stop new work; finish the mailbox.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="sequence-item">
                  <span>3</span><b>Persist</b
                  ><small>Save the latest actor state.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="sequence-item">
                  <span>4</span><b>Transfer</b
                  ><small>Atomically update Redis ownership.</small>
                </div>
                <div class="sequence-item">
                  <span>5</span><b>Activate</b
                  ><small>New owner loads state and resumes.</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="rebalance-foot">
                <span
                  ><i class="status-dot amber"></i> Ownership versions fence
                  stale workers</span
                ><span>Trigger from the Rebalancing page or runtime API</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section
            id="singletons"
            class="section-block split-section singleton-section"
          >
            <div>
              <div class="section-kicker">
                EXCLUSIVE COORDINATION <span>06</span>
              </div>
              <h2>One valid owner<br />at a time.</h2>
              <p class="section-copy">
                A singleton actor is useful for shared coordination, such as a
                global scheduler. Redis leases grant one worker ownership, and
                fencing generations make stale owners invalid.
              </p>
              <div class="lease-list">
                <div>
                  <i class="status-dot green"></i
                  ><span>Acquire a lease with an owner and expiry</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <i class="status-dot blue"></i
                  ><span>Renew while the worker is healthy</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <i class="status-dot amber"></i
                  ><span>Expire and fail over after worker loss</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="lease-card panel">
              <div class="lease-card-head">
                <span class="node-icon amber-icon">◇</span
                ><span class="badge online">LEASE ACTIVE</span>
              </div>
              <div class="lease-title">GlobalSchedulerActor</div>
              <div class="lease-id">singleton://global-scheduler</div>
              <div class="lease-divider"></div>
              <div class="lease-detail">
                <span>Current owner</span
                ><b><i class="live-dot"></i> worker-b</b>
              </div>
              <div class="lease-detail">
                <span>Lease generation</span><b class="mono">fence-018</b>
              </div>
              <div class="lease-detail">
                <span>Lease expiry</span
                ><b class="mono">renewed periodically</b>
              </div>
              <div class="lease-foot">
                If the lease expires, another healthy worker can acquire a newer
                generation.
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="kubernetes" class="section-block">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">
                  CLUSTER INTEGRATION <span>07</span>
                </div>
                <h2>Kubernetes runs the workers.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                ActorLab uses the Kubernetes JavaScript client for real cluster
                information and worker scaling. When no cluster is configured,
                the app reports local mode.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="kube-layout">
              <div class="kube-copy panel">
                <div class="kube-title">
                  <span class="kube-wheel">☸</span>
                  <div>
                    <b>Cluster adapter</b><small>@kubernetes/client-node</small>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Connects through kubeconfig during local development or the
                  in-cluster service account in Kubernetes.
                </p>
                <div class="kube-capabilities">
                  <span>List worker pods</span><span>Read pod status</span
                  ><span>Inspect deployment</span
                  ><span>Scale worker replicas</span
                  ><span>Read logs when available</span>
                </div>
                <div class="local-warning">
                  <span>i</span>
                  <p>
                    <b>No cluster configured?</b> The cluster page shows “Local
                    Development Mode” and no fabricated pod data.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="deploy-panel panel">
                <div class="code-head">
                  <span>DEPLOYMENT SHAPE</span
                  ><span class="badge durable">K8S</span>
                </div>
                <div class="deploy-tree">
                  <div>
                    <span class="tree-icon">▣</span><b>actorlab namespace</b>
                  </div>
                  <div class="tree-child">
                    <span class="tree-line"></span
                    ><span class="tree-icon api-tree">⌁</span
                    ><b>API deployment</b><small>Express + EJS</small>
                  </div>
                  <div class="tree-child">
                    <span class="tree-line"></span
                    ><span class="tree-icon worker-tree">▦</span
                    ><b>Worker deployment</b><small>scalable replicas</small>
                  </div>
                  <div class="tree-child">
                    <span class="tree-line"></span
                    ><span class="tree-icon data-tree">◉</span
                    ><b>Redis + MongoDB</b><small>coordination + state</small>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="deploy-footer">
                  <span>Minimal RBAC</span><span>Shared application image</span
                  ><span>Worker service</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="local-dev" class="section-block local-section">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <div class="section-kicker">GET STARTED <span>08</span></div>
                <h2>Run the runtime locally.</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                Start data services with Docker Compose, then run the API and
                workers as separate processes. Use the same application image
                for cluster deployments.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal panel">
              <div class="terminal-head">
                <div class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <span>TERMINAL · ACTORLAB</span
                ><button
                  class="copy-button"
                  type="button"
                  data-copy="npm install&#10;Copy-Item .env.example .env&#10;docker compose up -d mongodb redis&#10;npm start&#10;npm run worker"
                >
                  COPY COMMANDS
                </button>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-body">
                <div>
                  <span class="line-no">01</span
                  ><code><em>$</em> npm install</code
                  ><small>Install the application dependencies</small>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <span class="line-no">02</span
                  ><code><em>$</em> Copy-Item .env.example .env</code
                  ><small>Configure local connection settings</small>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <span class="line-no">03</span
                  ><code><em>$</em> docker compose up -d mongodb redis</code
                  ><small
                    >Start the durable state and coordination stores</small
                  >
                </div>
                <div>
                  <span class="line-no">04</span
                  ><code><em>$</em> npm start</code
                  ><small>Run the API and server-rendered UI</small>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <span class="line-no">05</span
                  ><code><em>$</em> npm run worker</code
                  ><small>Start a worker in a second terminal</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-foot">
                <span
                  ><i class="status-dot green"></i> Local runtime · Kubernetes
                  is optional</span
                ><span>Set a unique WORKER_ID to add workers</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="demo-callout">
              <div class="demo-symbol">↗</div>
              <div>
                <b>Follow an actor through the runtime</b>
                <p>
                  Create a CounterActor, send increment messages, restart or
                  move its worker, then confirm its saved count is restored from
                  MongoDB.
                </p>
              </div>
              <a href="#message-flow">SEE THE FLOW <span>↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </section>
          <footer class="footer">
            <a class="brand footer-brand" href="#top"
              ><span class="brand-mark">A</span
              ><span>Actor<span class="brand-light">Lab</span></span></a
            ><span>Virtual actors · Durable state · Kubernetes workers</span
            ><a href="#top">BACK TO TOP ↑</a>
          </footer>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>
    <script src="/assets/js/project.js" defer></script>
  </body>
</html>
